.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt MANET-REGION.PY 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm manet-region.py
.Nd write the configured regulatory domain to radio configuration files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm apply
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads
.Li regulatory_domain
from the node configuration and writes it to Wi-Fi, HaLow and
access-point configuration files.
Run as root after setting the country in
.Pa /etc/mesh.conf .
A missing or empty setting defaults to
.Li US .
The command accepts only the
.Cm apply
argument.
.Pp
Countries using the EU HaLow plan are mapped to the HaLow
.Li EU
domain.
Moving between US and non-US HaLow plans resets the HaLow channel fields
to the new plan's defaults.
The derived
.Li halow_regulatory_domain
is saved in the node configuration after the radio files are updated.
.Pp
Changed filenames are printed.
The command does not restart radios or reboot; radios use the configuration
from the next boot.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/mesh.conf
Configured country and derived HaLow domain.
.It Pa /etc/modprobe.d/cfg80211.conf , /etc/modprobe.d/morse.conf
Kernel module regulatory settings.
.It Pa /etc/default/crda
Userspace regulatory-domain setting.
.It Pa /etc/hostapd/hostapd.conf
Access-point country code, updated if the file exists.
.It Pa /etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant-*.conf
Existing Wi-Fi and HaLow supplicant country and channel settings.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after applying settings, 1 for a configuration or file error,
and 2 for invalid arguments.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Apply the country already selected in the node configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo manet-region.py apply
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr radio-setup.sh 8
